<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-gallus-gallus-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Gallus gallus Holocene Turing pigment-ocellus wavelength, 319.2 µm (pass 1) (Gallus gallus)",
        "Gallus gallus Holocene Turing pigment-ocellus wavelength, 319.2 µm (pass 1) faithfully reproduces Gallus gallus morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-gallus-gallus-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-gallus-gallus-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-gallus-gallus-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-gallus-gallus-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-gallus-gallus-turing-wavelength-s0.py, morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_3228_gallus_gallus_turing_wavelength_s0.lean implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Gallus gallus specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-gallus-gallus-turing-wavelength-s0.py>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_3228_gallus_gallus_turing_wavelength_s0.lean> ;
    schema:about "Gallus gallus" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: That a blinded prediction of a second feather was tested.",
        "does_not_claim: That pass 1 already contains a parameter sweep, an integrated ablation, or specimen CV segmentation.",
        "does_not_claim: That the painted bar measures 319.2 µm.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg slopes at (a, b) = (0.2005, 0.7995), Du = 1, Dv = 16, with γ solved so λ_c = 319.2 µm.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Single-harmonic radial reconstruction of the gallery ocellus plate, grown by a Stuart-Landau amplitude in a 12-frame GIF.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Singleton Holocene chronoseries: age 0 Ma, index 1 of 1, no predecessor and no successor.",
        "reported_in_source: Harris et al. (2005) reported Shh/Bmp2 activator-inhibitor interactions during barb-ridge formation in embryonic Gallus gallus.",
        "reported_in_source: Prum & Williamson (2002) reproduced within-feather bars, spots, and ocelli with reaction-diffusion on a growing feather germ.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing (1952) derived a finite-wavenumber instability of a homogeneous reaction-diffusion state.",
        "transfer_boundary: 319.2 µm is the slot's primordium-scale wavelength, not a length read off the plate's painted 100 µm bar.",
        "transfer_boundary: The gallery plate is the campaign ocellus image, not a micrograph with a calibrated scale." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Gallus gallus" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Aves (Ornithes)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Gallus" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-gallus-gallus-turing-wavelength-s0.py, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_3228_gallus_gallus_turing_wavelength_s0.lean; output: docs/media/gallus_gallus_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Gallus gallus; environment: python 3.12.3, note numpy, scipy, pillow, matplotlib, pyyaml, rdflib installed for this run; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing (1952) derived a finite-wavenumber instability of a homogeneous reaction-diffusion state. | Prum & Williamson (2002) reproduced within-feather bars, spots, and ocelli with reaction-diffusion on a growing feather germ. | Harris et al. (2005) reported Shh/Bmp2 activator-inhibitor interactions during barb-ridge formation in embryonic Gallus gallus.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg slopes at (a, b) = (0.2005, 0.7995), Du = 1, Dv = 16, with γ solved so λ_c = 319.2 µm. | Singleton Holocene chronoseries: age 0 Ma, index 1 of 1, no predecessor and no successor. | Single-harmonic radial reconstruction of the gallery ocellus plate, grown by a Stuart-Landau amplitude in a 12-frame GIF.; transfer_boundary: 319.2 µm is the slot's primordium-scale wavelength, not a length read off the plate's painted 100 µm bar. | The gallery plate is the campaign ocellus image, not a micrograph with a calibrated scale.; does_not_claim: That a blinded prediction of a second feather was tested. | That the painted bar measures 319.2 µm. | That pass 1 already contains a parameter sweep, an integrated ablation, or specimen CV segmentation.]; phenomenon_size: 358 µm (0.0003584 m, log10=-3.446 m, tier=5_primordium_100um); species_scale_ladder (22 runs from 358 µm to 80.6 cm): 358 µm:gallus-gallus-bioelectric-polarity, 691 µm:gallus-gallus-vertex-packing, 752 µm:differential-adhesion-sorting, 752 µm:gastrulation-streak-attractor, 1.3 cm:gallus-gallus-turing-wavelength, 2.2 cm:fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront, 2.4 cm:gallus-gallus-clock-wavefront, 4.5 cm:joint-interzone-clefting" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0500781102>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.2001.1896>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1001028> ;
